/-!
# From generation by one section on the small étale site to a principal defining ideal

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B` and let
`Z ⊆ X` be a closed subspace.  Stacks 083B(1) asks that the defining ideal sheaf `𝓘_Z ⊆ 𝒪_X` be
generated by one section locally on the *small étale site* of `X`.  On an étale chart `W` whose
underlying scheme is affine that hypothesis produces a single section `a` of `𝓘_Z` over `W` and
an epimorphism `𝒪_X|_W ⟶ 𝓘_Z|_W` of sheaves on the slice site, which says only that every
section of `𝓘_Z` becomes a multiple of `a` after a *further étale covering*.  This file closes
the gap between that and the ideal-theoretic statement

`𝓘_Z(W) = (a)`,

which is what the scheme-level theory of locally principal closed subschemes consumes.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_singleton_of_forall_chartAppTop`: **membership in a principal
  ideal of the ring of regular functions on an affine étale chart is local in the small étale
  topology.**  No hypothesis on the ideal, and in particular no finiteness: membership descends
  one element at a time.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt_eq_span_of_generatesLocally` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_eq_span_definingIdealAt_of_generatingSections`: **on an affine
  étale chart, a family of generating sections of the defining ideal sheaf indexed by a singleton
  generates the defining ideal there on the nose.**

## Implementation notes

The descent is faithfully flat descent of membership.  A covering sieve of an étale chart whose
underlying scheme is affine contains a *finite* family of étale charts with affine underlying
schemes which is still covering and which is an étale, hence fppf, covering family of the
underlying schemes (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_etale_ofArrows_le`);
the product of the rings of global functions on the members of such a family is faithfully flat
over the ring of global functions on the chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.faithfullyFlat_pi_gamma_of_ofArrows_mem_fppfPrecoverage`), because no member
need be surjective by itself.  Membership in a principal ideal then descends along that product
by `Stacks.Divisors.mem_span_singleton_of_map_mem_span_singleton`.

The algebra structures are the ones the faithful-flatness statement asks for, namely the
consumer's own: each is `RingHom.toAlgebra` of the map of global functions induced by the
morphism of charts, so the compatibility hypothesis holds by `rfl`.  For the same reason the
rings of sections are written as `Γ(·, ⊤)` of the underlying scheme of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.toOver`, and not through the projection of the chart:
instance search does not unfold a composite of functors, so the two spellings of one and the
same type are not interchangeable for it.

Generation by one section is used in the elementwise form
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.GeneratesLocally`, which an epimorphism out of the free sheaf of modules
supplies by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatesLocally_of_epi`; it is applied at the identity
morphism of the chart, so the covering sieve it produces is a covering sieve of the chart itself.
That a section of the defining ideal sheaf over a chart *is* a regular function on the chart
scheme lying in the defining ideal, that restriction of such a section is pullback of regular
functions, and that a multiple of such a section is a product of regular functions are each true
by definition, as in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/LocallyPrincipalPullback.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 083B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/083B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05AY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AY)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **Membership in a principal ideal of the regular functions on an affine étale chart is local
in the small étale topology.**  If the image of `t` under pullback of regular functions along
every arrow of a covering sieve of `W` is a multiple of the image of `a`, then `t` is already a
multiple of `a` on `W`.

The sieve is refined to a finite family of étale charts with affine underlying schemes which is
an fppf covering family in schemes, and the product of the rings of global functions on its
members is faithfully flat over the ring of global functions on `W`. -/
theorem mem_span_singleton_of_forall_chartAppTop
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (W : SmallEtale B S hS F)
    (hW : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj W)))
    (a t : Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj W), ⊤))
    (R : Sieve W) (hR : R ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS F W)
    (hmem : ∀ (W' : SmallEtale B S hS F) (g : W' ⟶ W), R g →
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).map g)).appTop.hom t ∈
        Ideal.span {((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
          ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).map g)).appTop.hom a}) :
    t ∈ Ideal.span ({a} : Set Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj W), ⊤)) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, z, φ, haff, hmemR, -, hetale⟩ :=
    SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_etale_ofArrows_le B S hS F hW hR
  have _ : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj W)) := hW
  have _ : ∀ i, IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj (z i))) := haff
  let alg : ∀ i, Algebra Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
        ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj W), ⊤)
      Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj (z i)), ⊤) :=
    fun i => (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).map (φ i))).appTop.hom).toAlgebra
  have halg : ∀ i, algebraMap Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
        ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj W), ⊤)
      Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj (z i)), ⊤) =
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map
        ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).map (φ i))).appTop.hom := fun _ => rfl
  have hff : Module.FaithfullyFlat Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
        ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj W), ⊤)
      (∀ i, Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
        ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj (z i)), ⊤)) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.faithfullyFlat_pi_gamma_of_ofArrows_mem_fppfPrecoverage
      (fun i => (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).map (φ i)))
      (Scheme.etalePrecoverage_le_fppfPrecoverage _ hetale) halg
  refine Stacks.Divisors.mem_span_singleton_of_map_mem_span_singleton
    (∀ i, Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
      ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F).obj (z i)), ⊤)) ?_
  choose c hc using fun i => Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 (hmem (z i) (φ i) (hmemR i))
  exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.2 ⟨fun i => c i, funext fun i => hc i⟩

variable (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS X.1)

/-- **The regular function underlying a section of the defining ideal sheaf over an étale
chart.**  A section of `𝓘_Z` over a chart `W` is a global regular function on the chart scheme
lying in the defining ideal there, and this is that function; the ascription is what keeps the
rings of the two spellings — the sections of the structure sheaf of the small étale site and the
global functions of the chart scheme — apart for instance search. -/
abbrev definingIdealFun {W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (t : ToType (((definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).toSheafOfModules).val.obj (op W))) :
    Γ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj W), ⊤) := t.1

/-- **A single section which generates the defining ideal sheaf locally on the small étale site
generates the defining ideal of an affine étale chart on the nose.**  The elementwise form of
generation says that every section of `𝓘_Z` becomes a multiple of `s default` after a further
étale covering, and membership in the principal ideal it generates descends along such a
covering by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_singleton_of_forall_chartAppTop`. -/
theorem definingIdealAt_eq_span_of_generatesLocally
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hW : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W.1.left))
    {I : Type u} [Fintype I] [Unique I]
    (s : I → ToType (((definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).toSheafOfModules).val.obj (op W)))
    (hGL : Stacks.SheafOfModules.GeneratesLocally (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1)
      ((definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).toSheafOfModules).val s) :
    definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op W) =
      Ideal.span {definingIdealFun B S hS X Z (s default)} := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun t ht => ?_)
    (Ideal.span_le.2 (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 (s default).2))
  obtain ⟨R, hR, hcoef⟩ := hGL W (𝟙 W) ⟨t, ht⟩
  refine mem_span_singleton_of_forall_chartAppTop B S hS W hW
    (definingIdealFun B S hS X Z (s default)) t R hR fun W' g hg => ?_
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hcoef W' g hg
  rw [Fintype.sum_unique, Category.comp_id] at hc
  exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.2 ⟨c default, congrArg Subtype.val hc⟩

/-- **A singleton family of generating sections of the defining ideal sheaf on an affine étale
chart exhibits the defining ideal there as a principal ideal.** -/
theorem exists_eq_span_definingIdealAt_of_generatingSections
    (W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hW : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W.1.left))
    (σ : (((definingIdealSheaf B S hS X Z).toSheafOfModules).over W).GeneratingSections)
    (e : σ.I ≃ Fin 1) :
    ∃ a ∈ definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op W),
      definingIdealAt B S hS X Z (op W) = Ideal.span {a} := by
  let _ : Unique σ.I := Equiv.unique e
  let _ : Fintype σ.I := Fintype.ofEquiv _ e.symm
  refine ⟨_, ?_, definingIdealAt_eq_span_of_generatesLocally B S hS X Z W hW _
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatesLocally_of_epi W σ.π)⟩
  exact Subtype.property _

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
